    "body": "Adds a config for [tex-ls](https://github.com/backmatter/tex-ls), a LaTeX and BibTeX language server written in Rust. It provides completion, navigation, rename, diagnostics, and code actions.\n\nThe main reason to choose tex-ls is its built-in formatting and lint fixes. It includes its own formatter and lint rules for LaTeX and BibTeX, without requiring latexindent or ChkTeX. The editor and CLI share the same lossless parser, formatter, and lint rules, so `tex-ls format --check` and `tex-ls lint` can also check projects in CI.\n\nThe config runs `tex-ls lsp` for `tex`, `plaintex`, and `bib` buffers, uses `tex-ls.toml` or `.git` to find the project root, and supports standalone files. [Installation instructions](https://github.com/backmatter/tex-ls#install) cover Homebrew and prebuilt downloads for Linux, macOS, and Windows.\n\nTested with Neovim 0.12.5 and the released tex-ls 0.1.0 binary: attachment and formatting for all three filetypes, project root detection, and standalone files. All five CI checks pass.\n",
